(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase458LedgerTruthAndWriteDiscipline"
  :createdAt 1789157400000
  :status "done"
  :priorityOrder 6
  :summary "Ledger Truth and Write Discipline: a certification cannot outrun its evidence, a commit message cannot claim a phase it did not close, two tasks cannot write one file unordered, and work in progress is never the only copy."
  :phase "Phase458LedgerTruthAndWriteDiscipline"
  :baseline "Measured 2026-09-11: commit 68d1e0b flipped a 48 gap ledger from action-required with 14 critical to certified-green with 0 open in a two line diff, while none of the 48 records carries a status field and 20 still carry critical severity; commits fa3f019 and 68d1e0b announce Phase 452 complete and Phase 453 certified while no Phase 452 or 453 task file exists and the roadmap ends at Phase448; the phase identifiers 450 to 453 exist only inside GAPS.asn and collide with the task file numbering; 529 pairs of planned tasks own the same file without any dependency ordering them, 450 of those pairs on asl/tools/asl.c; the asl submodule carried 674 kilobytes of uncommitted tracked change."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task45801"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-458"
      :title "A certification requires per item evidence, not a header edit"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "ledgerTruth"
      :state :done
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789157400000
      :motivation "The strongest claim in the repository, that 48 recorded gaps were all closed and none remained critical, was produced by editing one line. The body of the same file contradicts the header, and the audit that would have caught it, asl audit consistency, does not read GAPS.asn at all and reported all five dimensions reconciled. A verdict field that any edit can set is not a verdict, and three of the four remediation phases it certified are refuted by direct measurement."
      :purpose "A ledger verdict is derived, never written: it is computed from the per item records, each of which must carry its own status, the receipt that closed it and the command that produced the receipt. A verdict that disagrees with the items fails, and a verdict without items fails. asl audit consistency reads every gap and decision ledger, not only the ones it reads today."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Verdicts computed from per item evidence" "Per item status and receipt mandatory" "The consistency audit covers the gap ledger" "A header edit cannot change a verdict"]
      :owns [".asl/mem/decisions/GAPS.asn" "asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/grammar/verification-contract.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_audit_consistency"]
      :relatedSymbols ["concepts" "gates" "grading"]
      :invariants ["D52" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45705"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45801"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45801.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Setting a verdict to certified while one item remains open fails, naming the item." "An item marked closed without a receipt fails." "Reapplying the exact 68d1e0b diff to the restored file fails the audit."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45801" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Give every gap a status and receipt field." "Derive the verdict." "Extend the consistency audit." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task45802"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-458"
      :title "A commit may not claim a phase the ledger does not contain"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "ledgerTruth"
      :state :done
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789157400000
      :motivation "Two commits announce the completion and certification of Phase 452 and Phase 453. No task file for either exists, the roadmap ends at Phase448, and the identifiers live only inside a gap ledger. A reader reconstructing history from the log learns of phases that the plan never contained, and a reader reconstructing it from the plan never learns those commits happened. The git history and the ledger are two sources of truth that disagree, which is the condition the ssot rule was adopted to prevent."
      :purpose "A commit whose message names a phase or a task identifier is checked against the ledger: the identifier must exist, and a completion claim must correspond to a settled record carrying a receipt. Phase identifiers are unique across every ledger, so a pseudo phase inside a gap file cannot reuse a task file number."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Commit claims validated against the ledger" "Phase identifiers unique across all ledgers" "The 450 to 453 collision resolved" "History and plan reconcilable in both directions"]
      :owns ["tools/pre-commit.asl" "asl/tools/asl.c" ".asl/mem/decisions/GAPS.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["main"]
      :relatedSymbols ["git" "ssot" "anchor"]
      :invariants ["D52" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45801"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45802"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45802.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A message naming a phase absent from every ledger is rejected with the identifier quoted." "A completion claim without a settled record carrying a receipt is rejected." "Two ledgers declaring the same phase identifier fail the uniqueness check."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45802" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Index identifiers across ledgers." "Enforce uniqueness." "Validate commit claims." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task45803"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-458"
      :title "Serialize the 529 unordered writer pairs"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "writeDiscipline"
      :state :done
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "planner"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789157400000
      :motivation "Measured across the 79 planned tasks: 529 pairs own a common file with no dependency ordering either against the other, 450 of them on asl/tools/asl.c, 40 on asl/grammar/rpc.asn and 14 on scripts/install.sh. The parallel rule requires one writer per owned partition, and the plan as written satisfies it only if every task runs strictly in sequence, which contradicts the multi agent parallel development the same plan calls for. The condition is invisible today because nothing computes it."
      :purpose "Every pair of tasks owning a common path is either ordered by a dependency or partitioned so that the overlap disappears, and a planning check computes the pairs and fails on any that remain unordered. Ownership of a file by dozens of tasks is treated as a decomposition defect rather than a scheduling detail."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Zero unordered writer pairs across the plan" "Ownership partitioned below file granularity where dozens of tasks share a file" "The check runs whenever a phase is registered"]
      :owns [".asl/mem/roadmap.asn" ".asl/mem/tasks" "asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_audit_consistency"]
      :relatedSymbols ["parallel" "oneStep" "anchor"]
      :invariants ["D52" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45802"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45803"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45803.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Adding two tasks that own one path with no ordering fails and names the pair." "Ordering them by dependency clears the finding without changing ownership." "The check counts transitive ordering, not only direct dependencies."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45803" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Compute the pairs over the transitive closure." "Order or partition each." "Wire the check into registration." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task45804"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-458"
      :title "Work in progress is never the only copy"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "writeDiscipline"
      :state :done
      :priority :moderate
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789157400000
      :updatedAt 1789157400000
      :motivation "At the time of measurement the asl submodule held 674 kilobytes of uncommitted tracked change and the root held 35 kilobytes, representing several sessions of work whose only copy was the working tree. A concurrent session had already reverted a completed change once by checking out a submodule. The workspace is local by design and has no remote, so the usual recovery path does not exist and the working tree is genuinely the only copy."
      :purpose "Before any operation that can discard working state, and before any session begins mutating a tree another session is writing, a restore point is produced that captures tracked changes and untracked files, is addressable, and is verified restorable. The restore point is a precondition of the operation, not a habit."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["A verified restore point precedes discarding operations" "Restoration is exercised rather than assumed" "Concurrent sessions detect each other before writing"]
      :owns ["scripts" "tools/pre-commit.asl"]
      :targetSymbols ["main"]
      :relatedSymbols ["git" "edge"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "D81"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45802"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45804"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task45804.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A restore point taken over a dirty tree restores it byte for byte, untracked files included." "A discarding operation without a current restore point is refused." "A second session writing a tree already being written is detected before the write, not after."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task45804" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Define the restore point format." "Exercise restoration in a test." "Gate discarding operations." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])]
  :notes "The owner named git as part of what must be fixed. The defect is not the commits themselves but that history and ledger can each assert something the other denies, with no check that compares them.")
